<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Seckenheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1462</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz-diocesan-feud">Mainz Diocesan Feud</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Seckenheim was fought on 30 June 1462 near Seckenheim, now part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mannheim">Mannheim</a>, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz-diocesan-feud">Mainz Diocesan Feud</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a> Frederick I the Victorious defeated an allied army and captured its leaders, Margrave Charles I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a>, Count Ulrich V of Württemberg and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> George of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metz">Metz</a>, who had to pay heavy ransoms. The victory made the Palatinate the leading power on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-seckenheim.jpg" alt="Battle of Seckenheim" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MSeses · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_Battle_of_Seckenheim1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
